<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Town, Cayman Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Town is the capital of the Cayman Islands, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-overseas-territories">British Overseas Territory</a> in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-cayman">Grand Cayman</a>. A small port for much of its history, it grew rapidly from the 1960s as the islands became an offshore financial centre, and it is now home to hundreds of banks and thousands of registered companies as well as a busy cruise-ship harbour.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-town-cayman-islands.jpg" alt="George Town, Cayman Islands" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: rh43 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:96-124_S_Church_St,_George_Town,_Cayman_Islands_-_panoramio_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
